    "slug": "game-phys-epa",
    "markdown": "# Game Physics: Expanding Polytope Algorithm (EPA)\n\nWhile the GJK algorithm is highly efficient at checking if two convex shapes overlap, it only returns a boolean result (`true` or `false`). It does not calculate the **Penetration Depth** or **Contact Normal** needed to resolve the collision.\n\nTo find these values, physics engines run the **Expanding Polytope Algorithm (EPA)** immediately after GJK returns `true`.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Handoff from GJK\n\nWhen GJK detects a collision, it exits, leaving behind a final **simplex** (usually a triangle in 2D or a tetrahedron in 3D) that encloses the origin $\\mathbf{0}$.\n\nEPA uses this enclosing simplex as its starting point. The goal of EPA is to find the point on the boundary of the Minkowski Difference $A \\ominus B$ that is closest to the origin.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Simplex Expansion Loop\n\nEPA expands the simplex outward iteratively until it touches the boundary of the Minkowski Difference:\n\n1.  Identify the face (or edge in 2D) of the current simplex that is **closest to the origin**.\n2.  Calculate the unit normal vector $\\mathbf{n}$ of this face, pointing outward from the origin.\n3.  Calculate the support point $\\mathbf{s} = s_{A \\ominus B}(\\mathbf{n})$ along this normal direction.\n4.  Calculate the distance from the origin to the support point along the normal: $d_s = \\mathbf{s} \\cdot \\mathbf{n}$.\n5.  If $d_s$ is not significantly larger than the distance to the face, the face lies on the boundary of the Minkowski Difference:\n    *   **Penetration Depth ($d$):** The distance from the origin to the face.\n    *   **Contact Normal ($\\mathbf{n}$):** The normal vector of the face.\n    *   **Exit Algorithm.**\n6.  If $d_s$ is larger, the boundary lies further out. Split the closest face, insert the new support point $\\mathbf{s}$ as a vertex, and update the simplex (forming a new, expanded **polytope**).\n7.  Repeat.\n\n<div style=\"margin: 20px 0; text-align: center;\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 500 220\" width=\"100%\" height=\"220\" style=\"background: #141416; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #27272a;\">\n  <!-- Minkowski boundary -->\n  <path d=\"M 150 40 Q 80 110 140 180 Q 320 200 380 130 Q 340 40 150 40 Z\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#27272a\" stroke-dasharray=\"2 2\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" />\n  \n  <!-- Origin -->\n  <circle cx=\"210\" cy=\"115\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#ef4444\" />\n  <text x=\"180\" y=\"110\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11\">Origin (0)</text>\n  \n  <!-- Original GJK Simplex Triangle (ABC) -->\n  <polygon points=\"130,90 190,160 260,80\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" fill-opacity=\"0.05\" stroke=\"#fbbf24\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\" />\n  <text x=\"135\" y=\"130\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"10\">GJK Simplex</text>\n  \n  <!-- Closest Edge (BC) and normal n -->\n  <!-- Project origin to edge BC -->\n  <line x1=\"210\" y1=\"115\" x2=\"235\" y2=\"135\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-emerald)\" />\n  <text x=\"240\" y=\"145\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\">n (Normal)</text>\n  \n  <!-- Support Point S outside the simplex -->\n  <circle cx=\"310\" cy=\"165\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" />\n  <text x=\"320\" y=\"170\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\">New Support S</text>\n  \n  <!-- Expanded Polytope (ABSC) -->\n  <polygon points=\"130,90 190,160 310,165 260,80\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" fill-opacity=\"0.08\" stroke=\"#38bdf8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" />\n  <text x=\"210\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"11\">Expanded Polytope</text>\n</svg>\n</div>\n\n---\n\n## 3. Contact Manifold Generation\n\nOnce EPA identifies the closest face on the Minkowski Difference boundary, it extracts the contact details:\n\n1.  **Penetration Depth ($d$):** Equals the perpendicular distance from the origin to the closest face.\n2.  **Contact Normal ($\\mathbf{n}$):** Equals the outward-pointing unit normal of the face.\n3.  **Contact Point:** Calculated by mapping the closest face's support vertices back to the coordinate spaces of the individual shapes using barycentric coordinates.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Implementation Example (Python - 2D Concept)\n\n```python\nclass EPASolver2D:\n    def __init__(self, shape_a, shape_b, gjk_simplex):\n        self.a = shape_a\n        self.b = shape_b\n        # Copy the simplex returned by GJK (must enclose origin)\n        self.polytope = list(gjk_simplex) \n        \n    def get_closest_edge(self):\n        min_dist = float('inf')\n        closest_idx = 0\n        normal = (0.0, 0.0)\n        \n        n = len(self.polytope)\n        for i in range(n):\n            p1 = self.polytope[i]\n            p2 = self.polytope[(i + 1) % n]\n            \n            # Edge vector\n            ex = p2[0] - p1[0]\n            ey = p2[1] - p1[1]\n            \n            # Normal perpendicular to edge, pointing away from origin\n            nx = -ey\n            ny = ex\n            length = math.sqrt(nx*nx + ny*ny)\n            nx, ny = nx/length, ny/length\n            \n            # Distance from origin to edge: projection of p1 on normal\n            dist = p1[0]*nx + p1[1]*ny\n            if dist < 0:\n                dist = -dist\n                nx, ny = -nx, -ny\n                \n            if dist < min_dist:\n                min_dist = dist\n                closest_idx = i\n                normal = (nx, ny)\n                \n        return min_dist, closest_idx, normal\n        \n    def solve(self, tolerance=0.001):\n        while True:\n            # 1. Find closest edge to origin\n            dist, idx, normal = self.get_closest_edge()\n            \n            # 2. Get support point along normal\n            sa = self.a.get_furthest_point(normal)\n            sb = self.b.get_furthest_point((-normal[0], -normal[1]))\n            s = (sa[0] - sb[0], sa[1] - sb[1])\n            \n            # 3. Distance from origin to new support point\n            support_dist = s[0]*normal[0] + s[1]*normal[1]\n            \n            # 4. If support point did not expand the polytope further, we reached the boundary\n            if support_dist - dist < tolerance:\n                return normal, dist # Return contact normal and penetration depth\n                \n            # 5. Insert new support point, expanding the polytope\n            self.polytope.insert(idx + 1, s)\n```\n",
