    "slug": "game-light-spot",
    "markdown": "# Computer Graphics: Spotlights & Cone Blending\n\nA **Spotlight** is a light source located at a single 3D position that emits light only within a specific cone. This models real-world light sources like flashlights, streetlamps, or stage spotlights.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Cone Cutoff Angles\n\nTo define a spotlight, we need:\n1.  **Light Position ($\\mathbf{p}_{\\text{light}}$)**\n2.  **Spotlight Direction ($\\mathbf{D}$):** The central direction vector of the cone.\n3.  **Inner Cutoff Angle ($\\phi$):** The angle defining the core beam of full light intensity.\n4.  **Outer Cutoff Angle ($\\gamma$):** The angle defining the outer boundary. Beyond this angle, the light intensity is zero.\n\nTo determine if a surface fragment lies inside the spotlight cone, we calculate the unit vector $\\mathbf{L}$ pointing from the light source to the fragment, and compute the dot product between $\\mathbf{L}$ and the spotlight direction $\\mathbf{D}$:\n\n$$\\cos\\theta = \\mathbf{L} \\cdot \\mathbf{D}$$\n\n<div style=\"margin: 20px 0; text-align: center;\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 500 240\" width=\"100%\" height=\"240\" style=\"background: #141416; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #27272a;\">\n  <!-- Spotlight source -->\n  <circle cx=\"250\" cy=\"40\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" />\n  <circle cx=\"250\" cy=\"40\" r=\"18\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" fill-opacity=\"0.15\" />\n  \n  <!-- Central direction D -->\n  <line x1=\"250\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"250\" y2=\"200\" stroke=\"#71717a\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\" />\n  <text x=\"255\" y=\"210\" fill=\"#71717a\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"10\">Direction D</text>\n  \n  <!-- Outer Cone Boundary -->\n  <line x1=\"250\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#fbbf24\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" />\n  <line x1=\"250\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"350\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#fbbf24\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" />\n  <path d=\"M 250 40 L 150 190 H 350 Z\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" fill-opacity=\"0.05\" />\n  \n  <!-- Angles curves -->\n  <!-- Inner angle phi (15 degrees) -->\n  <path d=\"M 250 90 A 50 50 0 0 0 230 80\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#fbbf24\" stroke-width=\"1\" />\n  <text x=\"215\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"10\">φ (Inner)</text>\n  \n  <!-- Outer angle gamma (35 degrees) -->\n  <path d=\"M 250 120 A 80 80 0 0 0 200 100\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#fbbf24\" stroke-width=\"1\" />\n  <text x=\"180\" y=\"90\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"10\">γ (Outer)</text>\n  \n  <!-- Vector L to fragment -->\n  <line x1=\"250\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"210\" y2=\"170\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-rose)\" />\n  <circle cx=\"210\" cy=\"170\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#ef4444\" />\n  <text x=\"155\" y=\"165\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"10\">Vector L</text>\n</svg>\n</div>\n\n---\n\n## 2. Smooth Edge Blending\n\nIf we check only if $\\theta < \\gamma$, the spotlight edge will be a sharp, artificial circle. To create a smooth transition from full brightness to dark boundary shadows, we interpolate intensity scale factor $I$ using the cosine boundaries:\n\n$$I = \\text{clamp}\\left( \\frac{\\cos\\theta - \\cos\\gamma}{\\cos\\phi - \\cos\\gamma}, 0.0, 1.0 \\right)$$\n\nThis scales the light brightness smoothly from $1.0$ at the inner boundary $\\phi$ down to $0.0$ at the outer boundary $\\gamma$.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Implementation Example (GLSL Fragment Shader Spotlight)\n\n```glsl\n#version 330 core\nout vec4 FragColor;\n\nin vec3 FragPos;\nin vec3 Normal;\n\nstruct Spotlight {\n    vec3 position;\n    vec3 direction;\n    vec3 color;\n    \n    float innerCutoff; // Cosine of inner angle: cos(phi)\n    float outerCutoff; // Cosine of outer angle: cos(gamma)\n};\n\nuniform Spotlight spot;\nuniform vec3 objectColor;\n\nvoid main()\n{\n    vec3 norm = normalize(Normal);\n    \n    // 1. Calculate direction vector from light to fragment\n    vec3 lightVec = normalize(spot.position - FragPos);\n    \n    // 2. Calculate theta angle (dot product between light vector and inverted spot direction)\n    float cosTheta = dot(lightVec, normalize(-spot.direction));\n    \n    // 3. Smooth intensity blend calculation\n    float epsilon = spot.innerCutoff - spot.outerCutoff;\n    float intensity = clamp((cosTheta - spot.outerCutoff) / epsilon, 0.0, 1.0);\n    \n    // 4. Calculate standard diffuse lighting\n    float diff = max(dot(norm, lightVec), 0.0);\n    vec3 diffuse = diff * spot.color * intensity;\n    \n    vec3 finalColor = diffuse * objectColor;\n    FragColor = vec4(finalColor, 1.0);\n}\n```\n",
    "title": "Spotlights & Cone Blending",
    "tagline": "Cone boundary equations, inner/outer cutoffs, and edge soft blending calculations.",
