    "slug": "game-vis-shadow",
    "markdown": "# Computer Graphics: Shadow Culling & Caster Volumes\n\nWhen optimizing game rendering, we cull meshes that lie outside the camera's view frustum. However, if we apply this culling blindly to the shadow map pass, we introduce glitches: if a tall tree stands outside the camera's view but between the sun and the player, its shadow should still be visible on the ground. \n\nIf we cull the tree, its shadow will vanish or pop out. To prevent this, we use **Shadow Culling**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. The Shadow Receiver Volume\n\nTo determine which objects must be rendered to the shadow map, the engine constructs a **Shadow Caster Volume**. \n\nThis volume represents the region of space containing any object that can cast a shadow onto the surfaces currently visible inside the **Camera’s View Frustum**:\n\n*   **For Directional Lights:** We extrude the camera's view frustum backward along the light's direction vector toward the light source.\n*   **For Point/Spotlights:** We build a volume connecting the light's source position to the corners of the camera's view frustum.\n\nAny object whose bounding box intersects this extended **Shadow Caster Volume** must be rendered in the shadow map pass, even if the object is culled from the main camera view pass.\n\n<div style=\"margin: 20px 0; text-align: center;\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 500 220\" width=\"100%\" height=\"220\" style=\"background: #141416; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #27272a;\">\n  <!-- Camera Frustum -->\n  <polygon points=\"120,90 200,90 280,160 80,160\" fill=\"#10b981\" fill-opacity=\"0.1\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" />\n  <text x=\"140\" y=\"130\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"10\">Camera Frustum</text>\n  \n  <!-- Light Direction (Sun) -->\n  <line x1=\"420\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"70\" stroke=\"#fbbf24\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-amber)\" />\n  <text x=\"355\" y=\"35\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"10\">Sun Direction</text>\n  \n  <!-- Shadow Caster Object (Outside camera view, but casts shadow inside) -->\n  <circle cx=\"330\" cy=\"80\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" fill-opacity=\"0.15\" stroke=\"#fbbf24\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" />\n  <text x=\"300\" y=\"55\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"9\">Caster (Outside View)</text>\n  \n  <!-- Extruded shadow path intersecting frustum -->\n  <line x1=\"330\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"230\" y2=\"155\" stroke=\"#fbbf24\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\" />\n  <ellipse cx=\"230\" cy=\"155\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" fill-opacity=\"0.2\" />\n  <text x=\"210\" y=\"175\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"9\">Cast Shadow</text>\n  \n  <!-- Shadow Caster Volume bounds -->\n  <path d=\"M 80 160 L 250 30 H 450 L 280 160 Z\" fill=\"#ef4444\" fill-opacity=\"0.03\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"2 2\" />\n  <text x=\"300\" y=\"200\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"10\">Extended Shadow Caster Volume</text>\n</svg>\n</div>\n\n---\n\n## 2. The Shadow Culling Pipeline\n\n1.  **Cull Main Pass:** Perform standard frustum culling relative to the camera to generate the list of visible meshes to render.\n2.  **Generate Shadow Caster Volume:** Combine the camera frustum and light direction to form the shadow volume.\n3.  **Cull Shadow Pass:** For the shadow map pass, check all scene meshes against this shadow volume:\n    *   If a mesh intersects the volume, render it to the shadow map.\n    *   If a mesh is outside the volume, cull it from the shadow map pass.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Implementation Example (Python - Shadow Frustum intersection check)\n\n```python\nclass Plane3D:\n    def __init__(self, normal, distance):\n        self.n = normal # (x, y, z) unit vector\n        self.d = distance\n        \n    def is_outside(self, sphere_center, radius):\n        dist = (self.n[0] * sphere_center[0] + \n                self.n[1] * sphere_center[1] + \n                self.n[2] * sphere_center[2] + \n                self.d)\n        return dist < -radius\n\nclass ShadowFrustumVolume:\n    def __init__(self, planes):\n        self.planes = planes # List of bounding planes defining the volume\n        \n    def should_cull_caster(self, sphere_center, radius):\n        # The object is culled if it lies completely outside any single bounding plane\n        for plane in self.planes:\n            if plane.is_outside(sphere_center, radius):\n                return True # Out of bounds, safe to cull from shadow pass\n                \n        return False # Intersects the volume; must render to shadow map\n```\n",
    "title": "Shadow Culling & Caster Volumes",
    "tagline": "Preventing shadow popping artifacts using extended shadow caster volumes.",
    "category": "Game Developer",
