    "slug": "game-ai-goal-oriented",
    "markdown": "# Game AI: Goal-Oriented Action Planning (GOAP)\n\n**Goal-Oriented Action Planning (GOAP)** is an advanced AI planning architecture popularized by the game *F.E.A.R.* (2005). Rather than hardcoding transition rules between FSM behaviors, GOAP allows NPCs to dynamically build their own sequences of actions to satisfy specific goals.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Core Architecture Components\n\nGOAP decouples decision making into three main systems:\n\n1.  **World State:** A dictionary of key-value pairs representing the agent's current understanding of the world (e.g. `{\"hasWeapon\": False, \"hasAmmo\": True, \"enemyDead\": False}`).\n2.  **Goals:** Target world states that the AI wants to achieve (e.g. target goal: `{\"enemyDead\": True}`). Each goal is assigned a dynamically updated priority.\n3.  **Actions:** The pool of behaviors the agent can perform. Each action defines:\n    *   **Preconditions:** Conditions that must be true in the world state before the action can execute.\n    *   **Effects:** How the world state will change once the action is completed.\n    *   **Cost:** A weight value representing the energy or risk of performing the action.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Planning using A* Search\n\nTo satisfy a goal, the GOAP planner performs an **A* Search** in **State Space**:\n*   The nodes in the search graph represent hypothetical world states.\n*   The edges connecting the nodes are the Actions.\n*   The planner searches from the *Current World State* to the *Goal State* (or searches backward from the Goal to the current state), selecting the path of actions with the **lowest total cost**.\n\n<div style=\"margin: 20px 0; text-align: center;\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 500 240\" width=\"100%\" height=\"240\" style=\"background: #141416; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #27272a;\">\n  <!-- Start State -->\n  <rect x=\"20\" y=\"90\" width=\"100\" height=\"50\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" fill-opacity=\"0.1\" stroke=\"#38bdf8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" rx=\"3\" />\n  <text x=\"30\" y=\"110\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"9\">Current State:</text>\n  <text x=\"25\" y=\"125\" fill=\"#a1a1aa\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"8\">{\"hasAmmo\": false,</text>\n  <text x=\"25\" y=\"135\" fill=\"#a1a1aa\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"8\"> \"targetDead\": false}</text>\n  \n  <!-- Action 1: Find Ammo -->\n  <path d=\"M 120 115 L 175 115\" stroke=\"#fbbf24\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-amber)\" />\n  <text x=\"125\" y=\"105\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"9\">FindAmmo (Cost: 5)</text>\n\n  <!-- Intermediate State -->\n  <rect x=\"180\" y=\"90\" width=\"130\" height=\"50\" fill=\"#a855f7\" fill-opacity=\"0.1\" stroke=\"#a855f7\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" rx=\"3\" />\n  <text x=\"190\" y=\"110\" fill=\"#a855f7\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"9\">State 2:</text>\n  <text x=\"185\" y=\"125\" fill=\"#a1a1aa\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"8\">{\"hasAmmo\": true,</text>\n  <text x=\"185\" y=\"135\" fill=\"#a1a1aa\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"8\"> \"targetDead\": false}</text>\n  \n  <!-- Action 2: Shoot Target -->\n  <path d=\"M 310 115 L 365 115\" stroke=\"#fbbf24\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-amber)\" />\n  <text x=\"315\" y=\"105\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"9\">Shoot (Cost: 2)</text>\n  \n  <!-- Goal State -->\n  <rect x=\"370\" y=\"90\" width=\"110\" height=\"50\" fill=\"#10b981\" fill-opacity=\"0.15\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\" rx=\"3\" />\n  <text x=\"380\" y=\"110\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"10\">Target Goal:</text>\n  <text x=\"375\" y=\"130\" fill=\"#a1a1aa\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"8\">{\"targetDead\": true}</text>\n  \n  <text x=\"130\" y=\"200\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"10\">Plan: FindAmmo ──> Shoot (Total Cost: 7)</text>\n</svg>\n</div>\n\n---\n\n## 3. Implementation Example (Python - Simple Action Planner)\n\n```python\nclass Action:\n    def __init__(self, name, preconditions, effects, cost=1):\n        self.name = name\n        self.preconditions = preconditions # dict\n        self.effects = effects             # dict\n        self.cost = cost\n        \n    def can_execute(self, state):\n        # Action is executable if current state matches all preconditions\n        for key, value in self.preconditions.items():\n            if state.get(key) != value:\n                return False\n        return True\n        \n    def apply_effects(self, state):\n        # Return a copy of the state with effects applied\n        new_state = state.copy()\n        for key, value in self.effects.items():\n            new_state[key] = value\n        return new_state\n\n# --- Simple action pool ---\nactions_pool = [\n    Action(name=\"FindAmmo\", preconditions={\"hasAmmo\": False}, effects={\"hasAmmo\": True}, cost=5),\n    Action(name=\"ShootTarget\", preconditions={\"hasAmmo\": True}, effects={\"targetDead\": True}, cost=2)\n]\n\n# Current State\nworld_state = {\"hasAmmo\": False, \"targetDead\": False}\n\n# Manual Forward Planner trace\nplan = []\ntemp_state = world_state.copy()\n\n# Simple loop showing action pipeline execution\nfor action in actions_pool:\n    if action.can_execute(temp_state):\n        plan.append(action.name)\n        temp_state = action.apply_effects(temp_state)\n        \nprint(\"Constructed Plan:\", plan) # Output: ['FindAmmo', 'ShootTarget']\nprint(\"Final State Result:\", temp_state) # Output: {'hasAmmo': True, 'targetDead': True}\n```\n",
    "title": "Game AI: Goal-Oriented Action Planning (GOAP)",
    "tagline": "Dynamic action sequences planning, preconditions and effects, and state space A* searches.",
    "category": "Game Developer",
